# Optional: dedicated Solana RPC endpoint for read-only wallet balance/token reads.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and set the URL. Local dev works without it.
#
# Why you may want this:
#   - The official https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com endpoint BLOCKS browser
#     requests (CORS/403), so from a web app every read fails against it.
#   - The app therefore defaults to a CORS-enabled public node
#     (https://solana-rpc.publicnode.com), which reads native SOL reliably.
#   - BUT getParsedTokenAccountsByOwner (SPL / Token-2022 token balances) is an
#     expensive indexed method that keyless public RPCs generally do NOT serve.
#     To read token balances, point this at a dedicated RPC that supports it,
#     e.g. Helius / QuickNode / Alchemy / Triton (most have a free tier + key).
#
# Read-only only: this endpoint is never used to sign or send transactions.
# Do NOT commit a private key or a secret-bearing URL.
VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
